# Strict types

Never use bare `string` / `number` as Record/Map keys when a known set exists.

```ts
// ❌
const labels: Record<string, string> = { pending: "Pendiente" }

// ✅
type CommentStatus = "pending" | "approved" | "rejected"
const labels: Record<CommentStatus, string> = {
  pending: "Pendiente",
  approved: "Aprobado",
  rejected: "Rechazado",
}
```

Look for unions in `src/types/`, Drizzle schema enums/literals, and Zod enums. Avoid `any` and avoid `!`.
